  "id": "artifact",
  "term": "artifact",
  "definition": "In EEG or ERP recording, an artifact is unwanted signal activity that comes from something other than the brain process being studied, such as eye movement during blinking. This kind of contamination can spread into recorded channels and distort the analysis of ongoing EEG and event-related responses.",
